the hypothesis space
is where we need

01:09:38.241 --> 01:09:40.720
to focus and I think

01:09:40.721 --> 01:09:44.340
this a very interesting things
to model but it requires-

01:09:44.341 --> 01:09:45.040
&gt;&gt; But that's your focus.

01:09:45.041 --> 01:09:46.010
You are going to
solve that problem

01:09:46.011 --> 01:09:50.305
for us. Yes, I agree.

01:09:50.306 --> 01:09:53.970
&gt;&gt; I like to,

01:09:53.971 --> 01:09:55.270
just on that note,

01:09:55.271 --> 01:09:58.140
you come to the idea of
theory revision, right?

01:09:58.141 --> 01:10:00.820
As opposed to gradually
growing things,

01:10:00.821 --> 01:10:02.780
you talked about children
having causal theories.

01:10:02.781 --> 01:10:04.350
They often have causal
theories that are wrong.

01:10:04.351 --> 01:10:04.791
&gt;&gt; Yes.

01:10:04.791 --> 01:10:05.910
&gt;&gt; And you have
another example that

01:10:05.911 --> 01:10:07.370
completely changes
the theory, right?

01:10:07.371 --> 01:10:09.745
It is not like gradual changes
not repeated exposure.

01:10:09.746 --> 01:10:11.300
How does that fit
into this notion of

01:10:11.301 --> 01:10:12.550
just massive revisions of

01:10:12.551 --> 01:10:14.130
what the underlying
representation looks like?

01:10:14.131 --> 01:10:14.690
&gt;&gt; Well, I liked

01:10:14.691 --> 01:10:16.365
that question because I
don't have the answer.

01:10:16.366 --> 01:10:21.620
&gt;&gt; Yeah, you know that one?

01:10:21.621 --> 01:10:24.030
&gt;&gt; Right.

01:10:24.031 --> 01:10:28.355
So, the good news.

01:10:28.356 --> 01:10:31.060
So, here, I mean

01:10:31.061 --> 01:10:33.840
knowledge is at
different locations here,

01:10:33.841 --> 01:10:37.440
but in particular, there's
the mapping to representations.

01:10:37.441 --> 01:10:42.280
Then, there's this very
compact representation

01:10:42.281 --> 01:10:44.700
of how the things are
related in that space

01:10:44.701 --> 01:10:45.770
and sort of corresponding to

01:10:45.771 --> 01:10:47.665
the set of rules
if you want, right?

01:10:47.666 --> 01:10:49.440
And the good news is that,

01:10:49.441 --> 01:10:51.545
the set of rules is
very easy to change.

01:10:51.546 --> 01:10:53.150
That's where you can
do one-shot learning.

01:10:53.151 --> 01:10:55.570
This is where you can
completely change your view on

01:10:55.571 --> 01:10:58.455
something without having
to rewire everything.

01:10:58.456 --> 01:11:00.110
And that's connected to

01:11:00.111 --> 01:11:01.630
classical idea with
the idea that, "Oh,

01:11:01.631 --> 01:11:02.900
I can keep all my
rules except they

01:11:02.901 --> 01:11:04.480
change this one and now

01:11:04.481 --> 01:11:05.710
my conclusion is
going to be completely

01:11:05.711 --> 01:11:09.000
different where that
rules is relevant.".

01:11:09.001 --> 01:11:13.365
So, by factorizing
representation

01:11:13.366 --> 01:11:18.860
from facts and rules to
make things a little bit of,

01:11:18.861 --> 01:11:20.255
you know, grow sketch,

01:11:20.256 --> 01:11:21.690
I think makes it

01:11:21.691 --> 01:11:23.885
much easier to do what
you are talking about.

01:11:23.886 --> 01:11:26.325
Whereas, if it is sort
of hidden in the mush

01:11:26.326 --> 01:11:28.310
of one big neural net
that does everything,

01:11:28.311 --> 01:11:30.030
it is kind of difficult now to

01:11:30.031 --> 01:11:32.365
change your mind about
something specific.

01:11:32.366 --> 01:11:36.175
And the representation
is never wrong.

01:11:36.176 --> 01:11:39.660
It's just- It might be
insufficient to generalize,

01:11:39.661 --> 01:11:42.445
but it's never wrong. It's
just a representation.

01:11:42.446 --> 01:11:44.240
The actual facts
are represented in

01:11:44.241 --> 01:11:48.290
this top little set of

01:11:48.291 --> 01:11:52.765
rules if you want so I
think it facilitates here.

01:11:52.766 --> 01:11:54.415
Thanks for asking. I
hadn't thought about it.

01:11:54.416 --> 01:11:56.110
&gt;&gt; If you want to make

01:11:56.111 --> 01:11:59.035
a drastic change
with a few example,

01:11:59.036 --> 01:12:02.180
you need very low capacity.
If you have high capacity-

01:12:02.181 --> 01:12:03.680
&gt;&gt; That's right. That's
what I said. The top thing

01:12:03.681 --> 01:12:05.790
has very low capacity.
It's sparse.

01:12:05.791 --> 01:12:07.855
It only uses very few variables

01:12:07.856 --> 01:12:10.770
and hopefully it is somethings
trivial like linear.

01:12:10.771 --> 01:12:16.890
&gt;&gt; So, how is low capacity
tricked with deep learning?

01:12:16.891 --> 01:12:18.340
&gt;&gt; We all know that

01:12:18.341 --> 01:12:20.875
the deep part is
the representation, right?

01:12:20.876 --> 01:12:23.110
I mean everything
is deep learning but

01:12:23.111 --> 01:12:25.990
the part here that is
traditional deep learning is

01:12:25.991 --> 01:12:30.775
the mapping from say images

01:12:30.776 --> 01:12:34.715
or image sequences to
that representation space.

01:12:34.716 --> 01:12:37.720
And that is where most
of the capacity is,

01:12:37.721 --> 01:12:39.880
and that is where it's hard

01:12:39.881 --> 01:12:42.640
to learn and that's
where we don't do

01:12:42.641 --> 01:12:44.450
the job yet because
I think we're

01:12:44.451 --> 01:12:47.165
not putting as much
pressure as we should

01:12:47.166 --> 01:12:49.965
on the representation
to the abstract and

01:12:49.966 --> 01:12:53.125
to have these- well,

01:12:53.126 --> 01:12:54.690
easy that we can

01:12:54.691 --> 01:12:56.935
make predictions in
that space very easily.

01:12:56.936 --> 01:13:00.510
That is what this is saying.

01:13:05.580 --> 01:13:07.710
Yeah.

01:13:07.711 --> 01:13:09.190
&gt;&gt; So, we get that we have

01:13:09.191 --> 01:13:11.600
a unconscious state and we
put the attention goes to

01:13:11.601 --> 01:13:13.530
a conscious state too but make

01:13:13.531 --> 01:13:16.210
up getting more broader concept.

01:13:16.211 --> 01:13:17.275
So, does the unconscious state

01:13:17.276 --> 01:13:18.905
encode all the
world information?

01:13:18.906 --> 01:13:19.660
&gt;&gt; All the what?

01:13:19.661 --> 01:13:22.060
&gt;&gt; All world information.
Or is it specific to the-

01:13:22.061 --> 01:13:23.080
&gt;&gt; All the world information?

01:13:23.081 --> 01:13:23.800
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

01:13:23.801 --> 01:13:26.310
&gt;&gt; Like, for example,
colors. So, I want to paint-

01:13:26.311 --> 01:13:28.720
&gt;&gt; Pretty much everything
that you can name, right?

01:13:28.721 --> 01:13:29.960
So even low-level stuff.

01:13:29.961 --> 01:13:32.300
If you ask me like what does
the color of that pixel,

01:13:32.301 --> 01:13:34.485
I can like pay attention
to it and tell you.

01:13:34.486 --> 01:13:40.165
&gt;&gt; So the input has to be
from different domains.

01:13:40.166 --> 01:13:44.775
&gt;&gt; Yeah. It's very rich,
this unconscious state.

01:13:44.776 --> 01:13:46.060
But mostly it is interesting

01:13:46.061 --> 01:13:47.180
not because it has the pixels,

01:13:47.181 --> 01:13:52.550
but because it has
the higher level things. Yeah.

01:13:52.551 --> 01:13:56.720
&gt;&gt; That's it. This notion
that we can only can put

01:13:56.721 --> 01:13:58.870
maybe save things in our memory
prove interesting that

01:13:58.871 --> 01:14:01.030
you see this as a
good prior or not.

01:14:01.031 --> 01:14:01.336
&gt;&gt; Yes.

01:14:01.336 --> 01:14:02.030
&gt;&gt; Bug of our brain.

01:14:02.031 --> 01:14:02.565
&gt;&gt; That's right.

01:14:02.566 --> 01:14:04.500
&gt;&gt; But there's a bunch
of other things

01:14:04.501 --> 01:14:06.760
where kind of irrational
or we're not good at

01:14:06.761 --> 01:14:08.980
handling like vastly
different skills and

01:14:08.981 --> 01:14:12.030
we act in kind of irrational
ways and I wonder if any of

01:14:12.031 --> 01:14:14.650
those would also be
interesting priors for dealing

01:14:14.651 --> 01:14:15.950
with the real world
as opposed to

01:14:15.951 --> 01:14:17.580
seeing them as kind of
failures of our breed.

01:14:17.581 --> 01:14:19.210
&gt;&gt; Well, maybe.

01:14:19.211 --> 01:14:21.805
But I think we have
to try to think

01:14:21.806 --> 01:14:23.160
of how they could be useful from

01:14:23.161 --> 01:14:24.620
a machine learning point
of view and then say,

01:14:24.621 --> 01:14:26.695
"Ah, maybe we could use this.

01:14:26.696 --> 01:14:29.385
It's a meaningful thing
to add and not just, "Oh,

01:14:29.386 --> 01:14:30.740
let's shoot
ourselves in the legs

01:14:30.741 --> 01:14:33.125
because humans have
that failure as well."

01:14:33.126 --> 01:14:37.270
&gt;&gt; Right. But I think
it can be useful

01:14:37.271 --> 01:14:38.950
that the roads are
really complicated and we

01:14:38.951 --> 01:14:40.730
need to build the- as humans,

01:14:40.731 --> 01:14:41.880
act in that world

01:14:41.881 --> 01:14:43.200
and we're trying to
reproduce that, right?

01:14:43.201 --> 01:14:44.470
&gt;&gt; And so some of
these things might be

01:14:44.471 --> 01:14:45.885
necessary sort of priors.

01:14:45.886 --> 01:14:47.460
Just to be able to
learn quickly enough.

01:14:47.461 --> 01:14:47.741
&gt;&gt; Right.

01:14:47.741 --> 01:14:50.875
&gt;&gt; For you to
assume or, you know,

01:14:50.876 --> 01:14:52.100
act as if you're
never going to have

01:14:52.101 --> 01:14:53.210
to deal with things that are in

01:14:53.211 --> 01:14:54.340
10 orders of two different

01:14:54.341 --> 01:14:55.510
skills at the same time
for instance.

01:14:55.511 --> 01:14:59.540
&gt;&gt; Yeah. But, we have
also to be careful,

01:14:59.541 --> 01:15:01.280
not to try to
reproduce everything

01:15:01.281 --> 01:15:03.075
that we know about
humans and the brain

01:15:03.076 --> 01:15:05.085
because some of
these things might be

01:15:05.086 --> 01:15:08.795
side effects of
our particular hardware or,

01:15:08.796 --> 01:15:10.880
you know, evolution
is imperfect and,

01:15:10.881 --> 01:15:12.800
you know, we like to
understand what we're doing.

01:15:12.801 --> 01:15:15.180
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

01:15:15.530 --> 01:15:18.460
&gt;&gt; Last question.

01:15:18.461 --> 01:15:26.355
&gt;&gt; So, I am curious about
what you're saying about using

01:15:26.356 --> 01:15:28.890
the low capacity
representation of the world

01:15:28.891 --> 01:15:32.160
for causal reasoning

01:15:32.161 --> 01:15:35.320
and reconciling that
with the fact that well,

01:15:35.321 --> 01:15:37.090
I mean, yes we we often have

01:15:37.091 --> 01:15:38.190
a very kind of abstract

01:15:38.191 --> 01:15:40.510
approximate reasoning
about the world.

01:15:40.511 --> 01:15:43.620
We know birds can fly for
example but then, oftentimes,

01:15:43.621 --> 01:15:44.865
when you're trying to really

01:15:44.866 --> 01:15:46.160
think through
a specific situation,

01:15:46.161 --> 01:15:48.625
the devil is in
the details, you know.

01:15:48.626 --> 01:15:49.036
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

01:15:49.036 --> 01:15:53.945
&gt;&gt; Do you think that
a good model would only use

01:15:53.946 --> 01:15:55.340
a single layer of low

01:15:55.341 --> 01:15:56.835
capacity information
or do you think there'd

01:15:56.836 --> 01:16:01.010
be some range of.

01:16:01.011 --> 01:16:04.490
&gt;&gt; So, I don't think that

01:16:04.491 --> 01:16:08.520
these abstract low
dimensional thing

01:16:08.521 --> 01:16:11.480
is the only space that
matters for reasoning.

01:16:11.481 --> 01:16:14.990
At each time we project
ourselves in in the future,

01:16:14.991 --> 01:16:17.320
when we think about something,

01:16:17.321 --> 01:16:20.190
all the low level stuff is there

01:16:20.191 --> 01:16:23.250
hidden and influencing
what's going on.

01:16:23.251 --> 01:16:24.740
So I think that's

01:16:24.741 --> 01:16:27.200
one reason why traditional
rule-based systems fail

01:16:27.201 --> 01:16:29.310
because they are
an incomplete description

01:16:29.311 --> 01:16:31.150
of what's really
going on whereas,

01:16:31.151 --> 01:16:35.035
we are able to use
our intuition along the way,

01:16:35.036 --> 01:16:37.210
which is hard to do with

01:16:37.211 --> 01:16:39.920
with pure symbolic
rule-based systems.

01:16:39.921 --> 01:16:42.410
So, by connecting
the low level stuff

01:16:42.411 --> 01:16:44.670
with the high level stuff
and keeping them connected,

01:16:44.671 --> 01:16:48.880
I think we can avoid that trap.

01:16:50.380 --> 01:16:58.930
&gt;&gt; Please join me in
thanking Mr. Wright.

